                       Cardgames

Various card games; til now they consist of:

  - Røvhult (the danish words for arsehole); obviously I learned it from danes
    (3 of them), but it is also known internationally.

  - Twopart: A game I learned from some norwegians. They probably mentioned the
    name; though I was not able to remember it (you have no idea how long it
    took me to learn the word "Røvhult" - not to mention the pronuncation).
    So the name describes the game (a bit).

  - Buraco: A famous game in Venezuela; a bit similar to Canasta or the like
    in Europe.

  - Machiavelli: Append your cards to the ones on the table without getting
    (too) confused while moving them around.

  - Hearts: A game included in various (?) versions of the operating (??? Well,
    sometimes) system from a company with a very good sales department.


Planned are:

  - Tarok. The game of my youth (long ago). Fucking hell, looking forward to
    the computer player.


