Card decks
----------

Are not included. But the configure process tries to determine, where the
KDE carddecks are installed and use those.

Of course you can also use other images; just make sure, that the cards are
numbered from 1.png to 52.png, starting with the ace of clubs (1.png), the ace
of spades (2.png), the ace of hearts (3.png), the ace of diamonds (4.png) and
then (in the same sequence of the colours) down from king, queen, ... to 3, 2.

The images for the front side must be put in a directory called cards-NAME
and the images for the back in a directory called decks (and must be called
deck#.png).

The path of the card decks to use can be specified with an option to
configure. If it is missing, the script tries to figure it out by itself.

Principally front and back of the cards should have the same size (as
otherwise flipping a card looks a bit weired).


Installation
-------------

See the file INSTALL


Documentation
-------------

Is in the doc directory; in HTML-format. If the documentation is properly
installed (make doc-install in the doc subdirectory; see also the file INSTALL)
or the path is specified either in the INI-file or via an option, it can be
accessed from the program (by pressing F1 or via Help - Content).


How to report bugs and/or send patches
--------------------------------------

Bug reports and patches should be send to the e-mail address of the author (me)
(g17m0@lycos.com).

Please include for bugs:

  - The version of the package. In case you don't know: The title of the
    about box.
  - The version of the used General library.
  - How to reproduce the bug.
  - In case of a crash there should also be a stackdump in your systemlog which
    might help in localizing the bug.
  - Anything else you think might be helpful.

Please note that I don't (can't) check my mails daily, so please be patient.
